<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">European integration</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">European integration is the process of political, legal, social and economic integration of states in or near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, brought about mainly through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a>. Earlier ideas of a united Europe looked back to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>, and in the interwar years Richard von Coudenhove-Kalergi and Aristide Briand argued for European unity. In 1951 six states, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-germany">West Germany</a>, placed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">steel</a> under the European Coal and Steel Community. The 1957 Treaties of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> created the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-economic-community">European Economic Community</a> and Euratom, the Single European Act of 1987 set up the single market, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maastricht-treaty">Treaty of Maastricht</a> established the European Union in 1993.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the twentieth century it became widely known as a destination for shopping, skiing and tax planning, and its later reforms show how a small society adapted to <b>European integration</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/andorra">Andorra · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>The Federal Republic became the anchor of <b>European integration</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/federal-republic-of-germany">Federal Republic of Germany · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>Luxembourg’s significance lies above all in its place in <b>European integration</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-luxembourg">Grand Duchy of Luxembourg · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>…Kingdom of the Netherlands turned a small trading nation with a vast Asian colony into a model of consensual parliamentary government and of the welfare state, survived German occupation and the loss of Indonesia, and became a founding pillar of <b>European integration</b> and a centre of international law.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Kingdom of the Netherlands · Into the Present</a></li></ul></section>
